{"searchParameters":{"hl":"en","type":"reviews","num":10,"page":1,"cid":"855637193957362546","engine":"google"},"reviews":[{"rating":1,"date":"a month ago","isoDate":"2026-08-04T08:19:52.168Z","snippet":"I am extremely disappointed with OpenAI’s customer support and billing practices.\n\nI accidentally ended up paying for two ChatGPT Plus subscriptions—one through Apple and one directly through OpenAI. I only intended to have one subscription.\n\nI contacted support because I wanted to keep my Apple subscription and have the OpenAI subscription canceled and refunded. Apple could not help because the duplicate charge was billed directly by OpenAI.\n\nThe biggest issue is that I never used the OpenAI subscription. I didn’t even know what email address it was linked to. I had to ask support to identify the account because I had no recollection of which email it was associated with. I couldn’t log into an account when I didn’t know what account it was.\n\nDespite explaining that this was an accidental duplicate subscription, OpenAI refunded only $4.91 of the $21.74 charge, stating that I contacted them 24 days after the purchase. That completely misses the point. This wasn’t a case of deciding to cancel after 24 days—it was a duplicate subscription that I never intended to purchase in the first place.\n\nI expected a company like OpenAI to make this right by refunding the duplicate charge. Instead, I was left paying for a subscription I never intended to have and could not even access because I didn’t know which account it belonged to.\n\nThis experience has seriously damaged my trust in OpenAI’s billing and customer service.","likes":1,"user":{"name":"Riana Canedo","thumbnail":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL6Foebon0aQTKXqoYMa0WzjulwbZQbgYAPRwyOdkrSidfGfg=s64-c-rp-mo-br100","link":"https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105373003698556319930/reviews?hl=en-US","reviews":9,"photos":0},"link":"https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m8!14m7!1m6!2m5!1sCi9DQUlRQ